SQL (Structured Query Language) is the standard language for querying a relational database. Products add extensions, but the core is shared.
SELECT Name FROM Student WHERE StudentID = 'S104';
SELECT Student.Name, Enrolment.Mark FROM Student JOIN Enrolment ON Student.StudentID = Enrolment.StudentID WHERE Enrolment.CourseCode = 'CSC101';
The first returns one column from matching rows. The second joins two tables on their shared key. INSERT, UPDATE and DELETE change data.
